{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"yes\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"During normal turning, significantly higher PMC-STN alpha coherence was observed in the TurnPre phase (p = 0.0045, Fig. 3A). In contrast, during turning freeze, there was an increase in PMC-STN alpha coherence (p = 0.048) and a decrease in M1-STN alpha coherence (p = 0.043) during the TurnStart phase (Fig. 3B).\",\n    \"The increased coherence between the PMC and STN may reflect a compensatory mechanism to maintain motor control in the face of disrupted cortical signals; however, this abnormal coupling could also contribute to the rigidity and motor impairments characteristic of FOG31,32.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"During normal turning, significantly higher PMC-STN alpha coherence was observed in the TurnPre phase (p = 0.0045, Fig. 3A). In contrast, during turning freeze, there was an increase in PMC-STN alpha coherence (p = 0.048) and a decrease in M1-STN alpha coherence (p = 0.043) during the TurnStart phase (Fig. 3B).\",\n    \"Our analysis revealed that the decreases in the PMC alpha power (β = 0.154, p = 0.035) (Fig. 4A) and increases in PMC-STN alpha coherence (β = 0.205, p = 0.006) (Fig. 4B) during the TurnPre phase, but not the TurnStart phase, significantly predicted the freezing duration within the trial.\",\n    \"A increased PMC-STN alpha coherence during the TurnPre phase (but not during the TurnStart phase) relative to walking predicted shorter freezing episodes.\",\n    \"PMC alpha power reduction during the TurnPre phase (but not during the TurnStart phase) relative to walking positively correlated with freezing duration.\",\n    \"A delayed and exaggerated increase in PMC-STN alpha coherence and concurrent decoupling of M1-STN alpha coherence was observed during the TurnStart phase.\",\n    \"The increased coherence between the PMC and STN may reflect a compensatory mechanism to maintain motor control in the face of disrupted cortical signals; however, this abnormal coupling could also contribute to the rigidity and motor impairments characteristic of FOG31,32.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法为部分支持，而非完全错误。原文确实明确报告冻结转弯时PMC-STN alpha coherence在TurnStart阶段相对于步行基线增加，也确实提出了该类耦合可能具有代偿作用、也可能参与FOG病理过程的两种解释。但是，报告如果不区分转弯类型，就遗漏了决定结果解释的关键条件：正常转弯时增加发生在TurnPre，而冻结转弯时增加发生在TurnStart。尤其重要的是，原文预测分析发现，TurnPre阶段PMC-STN alpha coherence增加与较短的冻结持续时间相关，而TurnPre阶段PMC alpha功率下降与较长的冻结持续时间相关。这些结果表明提前出现的耦合与较轻的冻结表现相关，具有潜在的保护性或代偿性意义；冻结转弯中的TurnStart耦合则表现为延迟出现的阶段性变化。指控者对这些原始研究结果的描述有明确全文依据。需要保留的限定是，原文没有直接证明提前耦合具有因果性的保护作用，也没有将延迟耦合明确命名为独立病理机制。因此，最准确的判断是：指控者对原文实验结果的概括成立；报告的说法有部分依据，但如果将TurnStart结果及其机制解释作为不区分正常转弯和冻结转弯的一般结论，就遗漏了重要限定，构成实质性的不完整解读。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "a66376fe-9913-4187-bf6b-3dc0c260d3d0", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261113T125426512397Z", "elapsed_seconds": 53.593, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T12:55:20.102175+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "5adfef4d5f5cb3ded875a4e950b9aba0963ec603dd50af2abe1a4e52a77c98de", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "yi/local-codex-auth", "account_sha256": "b3efb6361563c139233ed7b7ef61a7c9afe0bd48d4eb3525dbe31956b024d6da", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 